  "_about": "Who may answer a palace question. The lens is the question the palace asks of a page (lenses.json); the voice is whoever has answered it well, from any field. This roster is names, domains and works only — never pre-written quotes, so the reader still has to find and verify the actual line. It is a floor, not a ceiling: the open reading (prompts/quoter.md) looks first for a voice the palace has never heard, and falls back here. `answers` names the lens pages a voice tends to speak to; `palace` and `speech` point at a citizen's own page and its cited verbatim excerpts, which need no web check. Circles mirror the Four Pillars so the pool is not only philosophers.",
